# What `prettier --write .` must never rewrite.
#
# Measured 2026-08-25 against `npx prettier --check <path>` on a built working
# tree, because an ignore rule nobody measured is a guess about what a tool does.
# Two entries below are PROVEN — they flag files today. The rest are GUARDS:
# generated output that flags nothing at the moment and must not start.

# PROVEN, 1 file flagged. npm owns this format and rewrites it on every install;
# a reformatted lockfile would be reverted by the next `npm ci` and would produce
# a diff nobody authored.
package-lock.json

# PROVEN, 2 files flagged. Playwright run artefacts, git-ignored.
test-results/

# GUARDS — 0 files flagged today, listed so that stays true. Each is build or
# tool output that exists on a developer's disk after a normal day's work, so a
# local `npm run format` would otherwise be one prettier release away from
# rewriting thousands of generated lines. CI never sees them: the format check
# runs on a clean checkout, before the build.
dist/
coverage/
documentation/
playwright-report/
.angular/

# GUARD, and the one with teeth. These are the visual-regression baselines
# (playwright.config.ts sets snapshotPathTemplate to {testDir}/__screenshots__).
# They are PNGs, so prettier does not match them today — but nothing in this
# repository is allowed to touch a baseline as a side effect. Regenerating one is
# a deliberate act (`npm run e2e:visual:update`), per ADR-007.
e2e/__screenshots__/

# MARKDOWN, EXCLUDED AFTER MEASURING IT. Prettier rewrites `*emphasis*` to
# `_emphasis_` and pads table separator rows — rendering-identical, but a
# TOKEN change to prose rather than a whitespace one, and it was the only
# non-whitespace change in the whole reformat (48 lines in
# frontend/e2e/README.md, 32 of them emphasis markers). Documentation prose is
# governed by docs/REFACTOR-STANDARDS.txt, not by a code formatter, and
# rewriting it was not what this gate was asked for. Reopen deliberately if
# markdown formatting is ever ruled on.
*.md
